            not fire (index empty?) or the re-read was skipped
    --- FAIL: TestResolveDuplicatesReportsThePersistedSuppressedHash
    FAIL    budget2/internal/services/mcpsvc/admin  0.007s

That guard Fatals before the file comparison, so I ran MY probe in the same
reverted copy to prove the discriminating assertion -- reported vs the bytes on
disk -- also fails, rather than only the heuristic:

    PROBE reported suppressed_hash = "9f58fcc457d8ab90"
    PROBE persisted suppressed_hash = "file:checking.csv|2024-02-06|-25000|0"
    MISMATCH: reported "9f58fcc457d8ab90",
              persisted "file:checking.csv|2024-02-06|-25000|0"

Same fixture, same posted values, opposite outcome. The test is not one that
passes either way.

The test also drives the PUBLIC write path (mcp CallTool "resolve_duplicates"
via connect(), not the store directly) and the LoadData-before-save ordering is
supplied by the tool itself: resolve.go:115 `deps.load()` runs before
SaveDuplicateDecision at :155, which is what populates the StableID index
canonicalKey needs. Without it canonicalKey is a no-op, posted would equal
persisted, and the test's :385 guard would fire -- exactly the trap the test's
own comment names.

